+/*
+ * msm8974 is a hybrid of the two generations either side of it, which is why it
+ * needs its own version rather than aliasing one of them. The IP is the 8x16
+ * generation - CSIPHY is 0x200 at +0xac00 with a clk mux, the same as 8x16 and
+ * unlike 8x96's 0x1000 three-phase block - but the topology is 8x96's: three
+ * CSIPHYs, four CSIDs and two VFEs, with the VFEs at +0x10000 and +0x14000,
+ * which are 8x96's offsets exactly. Every offset within the CAMSS window and
+ * every interrupt number matches those SoCs; only the base moves, to 0xfda00000.
+ *
+ * The clock rates are msm8974's own, read out of mmcc-msm8974: CSI and the
+ * CSIPHY timers offer 100 and 200 MHz as on 8x16, but VFE has a longer table of
+ * its own rather than 8x16's.
